Ham::CW
=======

Morse code for Perl and the command line: text, timed keying events,
PCM WAV and MIDI generation, and experimental decoding of recorded CW.

Requirements
------------

Perl 5.20 or later and ExtUtils::MakeMaker 7.22 or later.
The default backend uses only core Perl modules. PDL 2.081 or later is
optional; performance depends on the operation and workload.
Core ExtUtils::Manifest is also required during configuration. Only module
paths listed in MANIFEST are installed.

Current development edition
---------------------------

Version 0.001, implementation 2168dbc, verified 2026-11-07.
All 12 required CI jobs pass, including Linux Perl 5.20, 5.34, 5.40 and 5.44,
macOS/Windows and current/minimum PDL. The ordinary suite passes 2,886
assertions in 33 files. Production coverage is 99.01% statements and
96.22% branches. Archive, isolated installation, CLI and examples pass.

Local paired measurements show 56-63% less Perl sample-generation time and
26-36% less WAV-generation time, with 72 unchanged sample/WAV fingerprints.
The dependency audit still reports pre-existing matches: two installed and
39 declared-range matches. No new advisory IDs were added against the
previous main revision. See README.md, docs/verification.md and
docs/security-ci.md for source hashes, dated evidence and limits.

Installation
------------

    perl Makefile.PL
    make
    make test
    make install

Use the make program supplied with your Perl installation. For a user-owned
installation, configure with INSTALL_BASE=/your/install/directory and add
its lib/perl5 directory to PERL5LIB. See README.md for details.

First commands
--------------

    ham-cw encode "CQ TEST"
    ham-cw decode -- "... --- ..."
    ham-cw wav --output practice.wav "CQ TEST"
    ham-cw receive --frequency 700 --wpm 20 practice.wav
    ham-cw help receive

Existing output files are protected. Use --overwrite for deliberate
replacement. Text is UTF-8; WAV and MIDI output is binary.
From a checkout, use perl -Ilib bin/ham-cw in place of ham-cw.

Documentation and limits
------------------------

    perldoc Ham::CW
    perldoc ham-cw

README.md is the repository overview. docs/README.md indexes the guides.
docs/usage.md contains recipes;
examples/README.md indexes independent runnable examples. The API reference
is installed as POD with each public module.

The repertoire follows ITU-R M.1677-1. Audio reception is experimental;
inspect warnings even when text is present. The library does not record a
microphone, play audio or control radio/MIDI devices. Benchmark and corpus
results are dated observations, not general accuracy or speed guarantees.

